  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.1. Increased capacity of member States to formulate and implement a new generation of gender-responsive national employment policies, including for youth</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The government formulated and finalized the Samoa National Employment Policy (SNEP) 2021-2025 in collaboration with the Samoan National Tripartite Forum (SNTF) and key stakeholders in response to country-specific labour market challenges and the socio-economic impact of COVID-19. Prior to the formulation of the SNEP, lessons from the SNEP 2016-2020 have been identified through a review.

Samoa has being elected by the International Advisory Board to be the Co-Chair of the Climate Action of Job Initiative (CA4JI) along with Spain. In April 2021, ILO host Samoa Climate Action for Job Initiatives (CA4JI) based on the Workplans of the Pacific Knowledge Sharing on Just Transition, Decent work and Climate Resilience in the Pacific Big Ocean States. The CA4JI has now finalized its work plan for Samoa. The ILO provided technical and financial support to the Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Labour (MCIL), the Samoan National Tripartite Forum and key stakeholders through a review of the Samoa National Employment Policy 2016-2020, the development of the SNEP 2021-2025, and support to strengthen the capacity for SNEP implementation.

ILO hosted the CA4JI for Samoa to reaffirm and validate the action plan by Pacific Bog Ocean States members in 2018, and screen under the CA4JI.

The ILO supported a rapid assessment on the Impact of COVID-19 on employment and business in  Samoa.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1.1. Number of member States with new generation of national employment policies addressing country-specific future of work challenges</narrative>
    </title>
